<title>SINGAPORE: Nepal awards Sept diesel buy tender at $176.99/T.</title>
<headline>Nepal awards Sept diesel buy tender at $176.99/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>State owned Nepal Oil Corp (NOC) has awarded its September diesel buy tender to German trader Mabanaft, industry sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>The level of the award was around $176.99 per tonne, on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis to the Indian east coast.</p>
<p>The tender sought 30,000 tonnes of 0.5-percent sulphur diesel for delivery September 21-30.</p>
<p>It closed on August 13 and was valid for two days.</p>
<p>In its last tender, NOC awarded two cargoes for August delivery, to major Shell Singapore at $162.69 per tonne c-and-f, and to Mediterranean trader BB Energy at $163.44.  </p>
